From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH mt76] wifi: mt7915: use smaller TX ring on Cudy WR3000H

The MT7915 driver uses a 2048-entry TX ring by default. On the MT7981,
a smaller ring is a useful performance experiment because it reduces
excess queueing in the Wi-Fi data path.

Limit the experiment to the Cudy WR3000H and retain the upstream default
for other MT7915 devices.

---
 mt7915/mt7915.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7915/mt7915.h
+++ b/mt7915/mt7915.h
@@ -22,3 +22,7 @@
+#ifdef CONFIG_MT7981_CUDY_WR3000H
+#define MT7915_TX_RING_SIZE		256
+#else
 #define MT7915_TX_RING_SIZE		2048
+#endif
 #define MT7915_TX_MCU_RING_SIZE		256
 #define MT7915_TX_FWDL_RING_SIZE	128
